I was experimenting with opencode for the first time and hit this too, I think they get clobbered by `messages_first` and `messages_last`.

This seems to help in `~/.config/opencode/tui.json`

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/tui.json",
  "keybinds": {
    "messages_first": "none",
    "messages_last": "none"
  }
}
```

> I had this same problem and had some **painful** back and forth with claude and eventually (sort of) solved it. I asked claude to summarise the solution and it gave the following (want to be open about it being AI):
> 
> 
> Had this exact thing on 1.17.11. Two separate problems stacked on top of each other for me:
> 
> 1. The provider doesn't auto-register even when auth succeeds — declaring it explicitly in config forces it to show up. Add this to your `opencode.jsonc`:
> 
> ```jsonc
> "provider": {
>   "github-copilot": {
>     "models": {
>       "gpt-4.1": {}
>     }
>   }
> }
> ```
> 
> After that the models actually appear and `opencode auth list` shows it connected.
> 
> 2. Heads up if you're on a student/free Copilot plan — since GitHub's March 2026 change, those plans can only self-select base models (gpt-4.1, gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini). Premium ones like Opus/Sonnet/GPT-5 return "model not supported" because GitHub gates them server-side behind Auto mode, so no config will unlock them.
> 
> Declaring gpt-4.1 in config and using that got me working.

This is great, thanks. Have you figured out any way to get the auto mode to work?

